                         BackGround & Purpose
                         ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
ConfTop was orginally written becouse it didn't exists any good door to count
uploads in a optinal conference under a choosen number of days. I orginally
got this idea from the WeekTop utility by AirWolf that counted the total uploads
in all conferences under a week. But since users started to ask me to code
something to count uploads in a special conference, i started coding this tool. 
The first version was coded in Arexx, and was pretty slow.
Now it's here, Coded in pure C and FAST!

As the sysop you are able to choose the interval (number of days), how many
rows (Uploaders) you want to show, and if you want to write any mail when
reseting. You can also choose if you want to write a bulletine. You may also 
have a headerfile/Tailerfile and a exclude-file for one or all conferences.
This are explained later in this document.

Since this door runs often, the computer of the board should be rather fast.
A 68000 Amiga is probably too slow to have any use for this tool, but on 020+'s
it should run fast enough.


                  To install Conference Top Uploaders
                  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
To install conftop on your amiexpress system, copy all necessary files into
an optional directory.

NOTE: IF YOU HAVE EXTERNAL PLAYPEN DIRECTORIES, YOU MUST MAKE A SPECIAL FILE.
      PLEASE READ LATER IN THIS DOCUMENT HOW TO DO IT!

Installation for amiexpress 3.0+ sysops:

Copy the included icon (Conftop.info) into the BBSCmd/ directory, and copy
(Filecheck.info) into SYSCmd/ directory. If you already have a filecheck.info
(for Bossnuke or whatever), copy it to BBSCmd/ and name it (Filechk.info) and
it will be launched after conftop have run.

NOTE: Remember to edit the path in Conftop.info and Filecheck.info, if you
      DO NOT put conftop in Doors:Amiexpress/Conftop/Conftop.X

------------------------------------- END OF AMIEXPRESS 3.0+ INSTALLATION

Installation for amiexpress 2.xx sysops:

Add this line to your BBS.CMD (or Customcommands).  (Use the included)

----Cut Here-----------------------------------------
*CONFTOP  XM010Doors:Amiexpress/Conftop/Conftop.x
----Cut Here-----------------------------------------
 ^^^^^^^    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |         |                 |> Filename of the door with full path.
   |         |>Accesslevel required to use door.
   |>The command that will invoke door.

Add this line to your SYS.CMD (or Customcommands).  (Use the included)

----Cut Here-----------------------------------------
FILECHECK XM010Doors:Amiexpress/Conftop/Conftop.x
----Cut Here-----------------------------------------

If you want to launch a door after (on amiexpress 2.xx), you must do a fake-
file named (BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/FileChk.info). You can just make it 0 bytes,
it doesn't mather. If conftop founds that file, it will try to start a door
called "FileChk" so you must enter this line in your BBS.Cmd (or Customcommands):

----Cut Here-----------------------------------------
FILECHK   XM010Doors:DUPECHECK.X
----Cut Here-----------------------------------------

------------------------------------- END OF AMIEXPRESS 2.xx INSTALLATION

Now, logon your local node and simply type: (Conftop -CFG). This will let you
into the configuration program where you can control everything.
(NOTE: Secuirty level 255 required for accessing Configuration menu)

When you have installed conftop into a conference with the config program,
you must load your texteditor (CED), and edit your bullbatch file in that
conference. (Ex BULL20.TXT or whatever)
(Use the included)

-------( Cut Here )----------------------------
~
Updating CONFTOP, please wait ~N ..
~CC_Conftop
-------( Cut Here )----------------------------


                          Configuration
                          ~~~~~~~~~~~~~
When you have installed conftop in your board (as described above), you must
join the conference you want to run conftop in. Enter "CONFTOP -CFG" and it
will let you entering the configuration program......

»thE EaSt BBS« [2:»CoMmOdOrE aMiGa«] Menu (60 mins. left): CONFTOP -CFG

A big configuration screen will be shown...

.----------------------------------------------------------------------------.
| Conference Top Uploaders -- Configuration Editor -- Security 255 Required! |
|--------------------------------------v-------------------------------------|
| 1) Number of Days : (   7)           | S) Save config.                     |
| 2) Number of Rows : (  10)           | L) Load config.                     |
| 3) Show Statistics: ( Yes)           | R) Remove conftop from conference.  |
| 4) Mail User      : (EALL          ) | A) About conference top uploaders.  |
| 5) Bulletin file  : (BBS2:Bulletins) | E) Edit users in datafile.          |
|                                      |                                     |
| Next reset: Fri Jan 07 00:00:00 1994 | Date     : Thu Dec 30 22:26:55 1993 |
|--------------------------------------^-------------------------------------|
| Please select (1,2,3,4,S,L,R,A,E) ?                                        |
|----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Configuration File not found. Using defaults...                            |
`----------------------------------------------------------------------------'

Now make the changes you want to do in the config.

( 1) - Change the interval (1-99). Conftop will always run continuos, which
       means after the choosen interval, conftop will start over and run
       again.
( 2) - Change the number rows (1-99). This is how many uploaders you want to
       show when a user is joining a conference.
( 3) - Change if you want to show statistics after conftop have reseted.
       It will show the top uploader last period and the record uploader.
( 4) - Change who you want to send a message to, or if you don't want to send
       any message at all. The message will be written public from user number
       one (Often the sysop).
( 5) - Change the name and path to the bulletine file that will be written each
       time conftop resets. Write 'NONE' to not make any bulletine.
( S) - Save the config.
( L) - Loads the config.
( R) - Removes (uninstall) conftop from this conference. All datafiles are
       are removed.
( A) - About conftop screen.
( E) - Let's you go to the user editor. The following screen will be shown:

.----------------------------------------------------------------------------.
|     Conference Top Uploaders -- Configuration Editor -- User Editor!       |
|--------------------------------------v-------------------------------------|
| 1) Username:                         | A) Add a user to datafile.          |
| 2) Location:                         | R) Remove a user from datafile.     |
| 3) Bytes   :                         | E) Edit a user in datafile.         |
| 4) Files   :                         | L) List all users in datafile.      |
|                                      | Q) Quit back to menu.               |
| S) Save datafile with all changes.   |                                     |
|                                      | Users in datafile: (  0)            |
|--------------------------------------^-------------------------------------|
| Please select (A,R,E,L,Q,S) ?                                              |
|----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Awaiting Command...                                                        |
`----------------------------------------------------------------------------'

( A) - Add a user to datafile.
( R) - Remove a user from datafile.
( E) - Edit a user in datafile.
( L) - List all users in datafile.
( Q) - Quit back to the mainmenu.
( S) - Save all your changes.

NOTE: The commands 'R,E & L' are disabled when no users exists in datafile.


     WE ARE VERY SORRY FOR HOLDING CONFTOP FROM RELEASE SOO LONG TIME,
        BUT WE WANTED IT TO BE THE BEST CONFERENCE WEEKTOP UTILITY
               AVAILIBLE FOR AMIEXPRESS BBS!  NOW USE IT!!


     How to run conftop if you have external playpen directories
     ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
If you don't have your playpen directories located in your NodeX directory,
you MUST make a file called "CONFTOP.PLAYPEN" and put it in BBS:

In this file you should enter which nodes who have external playpen dirs >:

-------( Cut Here )----------------------------
NODE1 RAM:PLAYPEN1/
NODE2 RAM:PLAYPEN2/
NODE3 HD0:PLAYPEN3/
-------( Cut Here )----------------------------

This means that if a user is uploading at node 1, conftop will search in
RAM:PLAYPEN1/ for the file. If the node is not listed, or the this file
doesn't exists, conftop will search in the normal BBS:NodeX/Playpen/ dir.

NOTE: DON'T REMEMBER TO ENTER THE SLASH OR COLON AT THE END!


                   How to exclude users from conftop
                   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Conftop will always search for a exclude file..

· Conftop.Exclude - with users to exclude from Conftop.

That file are first searched for in the conference path (ex BBS:Elite/), and
if it is not found, it will search in BBS:. If the user is found in exclude
file, conftop will not update him in the datafile when he upload files.


                          Use a Header/Tailer
                          ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Conftop will always search for a headerfile/tailerfile ..

· Conftop.Header - for display before the output, and
· Conftop.Tailer - for display after the output.

These files are first looked for in the conference path (ex BBS:Elite/), and
if it is not found, it will search in BBS:. If no headerfile is found, a
clear-screen (CTRL-L) is sent so it displays quicker/nicer.

NOTE: When you are using a own headerfile, don't forget the clear-screen at
      the top!


                         In futher versions
                         ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
In futher versions, Conftop will be run via icons. All information will be
stored there, which means that the program size will be ALOT smaller! (Since
the config prg can be removed). You will also be able to configable a start-
date for use if you are going to use conftop in competions. Conftop will also
be more optimized, and i have a new design that maybe will be used.

More ideas wanted for future releases! Call my board today!


